title: The Cabinet of Business
subtitle: The coalition breaks over the eight-hour day.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 11
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_labour_branch = (Q.kapp_outcome == 3) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e22_old_chancellor = Q.chancellor;
var cuno = function () {
    Q.government_name = 'Cuno cabinet (non-party, with Centre, DDP, DVP, BVP)';
    Q.chancellor = 'Wilhelm Cuno';
    Q.spd_in_government = 0; Q.zentrum_in_government = 1; Q.ddp_in_government = 1; Q.dvp_in_government = 1; Q.bvp_in_government = 1;
    Q.e22_workers_gov = 0;
};
if (!Q.e22_labour_branch) {
    cuno();
    RG.news('Cuno forms a cabinet of business', 3);
}
!}

= The Cabinet of Business

[? if e22_labour_branch = 0 : On 14 November Chancellor [+ e22_old_chancellor +] resigns. The People's Party would join a broad coalition only if the SPD gave up the eight-hour day, and the SPD would not. A week later Ebert appoints Wilhelm Cuno, director of the Hamburg-America Line, at the head of a cabinet of shipowners, bankers and officials. The SPD goes into opposition. ?]

[? if e22_labour_branch = 1 : The workers' government born in the strike against Kapp is in danger. The Centre and the Democrats, who have tolerated it for two years, now want the eight-hour day suspended and the reparations handed to men of business. Without them it has no majority unless our deputies vote for it. Behind the scenes the shipowner Wilhelm Cuno is already named as the bankers' candidate. ?]

- @poster: Campaign against the government of Stinnes.
- @spd: Ask the SPD to fight Cuno with us.
- @tolerate: Keep the workers' government in office with our votes.
- @enter: Enter the workers' government.
- @let_fall: Let it fall.

@poster
subtitle: Our posters against theirs.
view-if: e22_labour_branch = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Our posters show Cuno and Stinnes counting money over a worker's coffin. They are pasted over by morning and pasted up again by night.

@spd
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The SPD is in opposition too. Its executive may not listen; its deputies might.
view-if: e22_labour_branch = 0
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any proposal to the SPD.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.spd_relation += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The SPD executive declines a joint campaign, but its Reichstag group votes with ours against Cuno's first decrees.

@tolerate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The workers' government survives, and we share the blame for what it does.
view-if: e22_labour_branch = 1
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids keeping social democrats in office.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
RG.news('The workers\' government survives by eleven votes', 3);
RG.ecci('radek', 5);
Q.e22_workers_gov = 1;
Q.government_name = 'Workers\' government (SPD, with communist support)';
Q.spd_in_government = 1; Q.zentrum_in_government = 0; Q.ddp_in_government = 0; Q.dvp_in_government = 0; Q.bvp_in_government = 0;
Q.spd_relation += 8;
Q.stability -= 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The government survives by eleven votes. The nationalist press calls the Chancellor a prisoner of Moscow, and the Reichswehr ministry stops answering his letters promptly.

@enter
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Communist ministers in Berlin. Zinoviev is appalled, and so is Seeckt.
view-if: e22_labour_branch = 1
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2 and spd_relation >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD will not take communist ministers.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
RG.news('Communist ministers in the Reich government', 3);
RG.ledger('Communist ministers sat in the Reich government.', 'e22_kpd_ministers');
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -8);
Q.e22_workers_gov = 2;
Q.government_name = 'Workers\' government (SPD and KPD)';
Q.spd_in_government = 1; Q.zentrum_in_government = 0; Q.ddp_in_government = 0; Q.dvp_in_government = 0; Q.bvp_in_government = 0;
Q.army_loyalty -= 8;
Q.stability -= 8;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
!}

Three communists take ministries: labour, food supply and justice. The first decree requisitions hoarded grain. The second dissolves the Organisation Consul. General von Seeckt calls on the President to say the army cannot answer for its mood.

@let_fall
subtitle: Cuno comes, and the SPD will not forgive us.
view-if: e22_labour_branch = 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Communist votes bring down the workers\' government', 3);
RG.ledger('The party brought down the workers\' government.', 'e22_let_fall');
RG.ecci('radek', -8);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 4);
Q.e22_workers_gov = 0;
Q.government_name = 'Cuno cabinet (non-party, with Centre, DDP, DVP, BVP)';
Q.chancellor = 'Wilhelm Cuno';
Q.spd_in_government = 0; Q.zentrum_in_government = 1; Q.ddp_in_government = 1; Q.dvp_in_government = 1; Q.bvp_in_government = 1;
Q.spd_relation -= 15;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Our deputies vote with the nationalists and the workers' government falls. On 22 November Cuno forms his cabinet of business. In the SPD's districts our members are spat at in the street.
